mmons licensing. Non-profit organisations and platforms are free to republish any single item we have published under a…\n- [Donate to openDemocracy](https://www.opendemocracy.net/tip-jar.md)\n- [Who Funds Us?](https://www.opendemocracy.net/who-funds-us.md) - We are extremely grateful to all our funders and donors, whose generous support allows us to continue producing high-quality journalism which challenges power, inspires change and builds leadership among groups underrepresented in the media. The support we receive through the generosity of our read…\n- [Write For Us](https://www.opendemocracy.net/write-for-us.md) - Writing for openDemocracy openDemocracy is an independent global media organisation. Through reporting and analysis of social and political issues, we seek to educate citizens to challenge power and encourage democratic debate across the world. We publish written and multimedia content primarily co…\n- [Writers](https://www.opendemocracy.net/writers.md)\n\n## Posts\n- [¿Lula o Bolsonaro? Brasil vota bajo la amenaza de Trump](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/brasil-lula-bolsonaro-golpe-trump-democracia-desarrollo-subordinacion.md) - OPINIÓN: El programa de Flávio Bolsonaro, que es el de Washington, equivale a una economía subordinada y confinada en la esfera de influencia de EEUU\n- [Tactical votes and soft Tories: How to keep Reform out of Number 10](https://www.opendemocracy.net/how-to-stop-reform-winning-next-election-farage-tactical-voting-andy-burnham-labour-hope-soft-tories.md) - Mobilising an anti-Reform voter coalition takes work, information, and community building, says Hope Not Hate\n- [When it comes to Palestine, it is governments vs. citizens](https://www.opendemocracy.net/weekly-email-260926.md) - openDemocracy Weekly Newsletter 26 September 2026\n- [El Proyecto 2025 de Trump refuerza a la ultraderecha en América Latina](https://www.opendemocracy.net/el-proyecto-2025-de-trump-refuerza-a-la-ultraderecha-en-america-latina.md) - Newsletter semanal correspondiente al 25 de setiembre de 2026\n- [Activistas por Palestina resisten en huelga de hambre en una cárcel de Túnez](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/palestina-tunez-solidaridad-carcel-huelga-de-hambre-flotilla-israel-gaza.md) - La vida de varios activistas encarcelados pende de un hilo en Túnez\n- [La sombra de Irán y francotiradores en Washington: el peligroso desmoronamiento de Trump](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/trump-iran-tension-washington-elecciones-medio-mandato.md) - El desastre militar en Irán y una capital blindada revelan a un presidente que se queda sin margen a medida que se acercan las elecciones de mitad de mandato\n- [A radical proposal to solve the housing crisis: Expropriation](https://www.opendemocracy.net/what-if-tenants-not-landlords-controlled-berlins-housing.md) - In Berlin, a campaign to expropriate housing from corporate landlords is winning widespread support.\n- [La ultraderecha latinoamericana se sube al Proyecto 2025 de Trump](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/heritage-trump-ultraderecha-latinoamerica-milei-kast-delaespriella-democracia-autoritarismo.md) - El autoritarismo del Proyecto 2025 gana fuerza en América Latina, impulsado por aliados de Trump y redes de ultraderecha tejidas desde hace años\n- [Around the world, people fight for Palestine as authorities crack down](https://www.opendemocracy.net/around-the-world-people-fight-for-palestine-as-authorities-crack-down.md) - In Tunisia, imprisoned Palestinian rights activists are on the brink of death.\n- [Iran threats and snipers in Washington: Trump’s dangerous unravelling](https://www.opendemocracy.net/iran-threats-and-snipers-in-washington-trumps-dangerous-unravelling.md) - Depleted missiles abroad and armed fortresses at home reveal a president running out of options as midterms loom\n- [Las Malvinas vs. the Falklands: Argentina's far right has weaponised the battle over memory](https://www.opendemocracy.net/falklands-malvinas-argentina-milei-far-right-weaponised-authoritian-measures-launder-military-reputation.md) - Milei is using dispute to impose authoritarian measures, while his vice-president seeks to launder military's reputation\n- [Exposing Palantir: Defence Contracts, Stock-Based Compensation, and Tax Avoidance](https://www.opendemocracy.net/exposing-palantir-defence-contracts-stock-based-compensation-and-tax-avoidance.md) - Despite reporting 55% profit margins and over $1.6 billion in net income, Palantir maintains an effective global tax rate of just 1.4% and pays zero federal income tax in the United States.\n- [Reform’s £72m ‘gift’, data centres, and the German far right](https://www.opendemocracy.net/weekly-email-190926.md) - openDemocracy Weekly Newsletter 12 September 2026\n- [Milei prueba con Malvinas el populismo nacionalista. ¿Qué puede salir mal?](https://www.opendemocracy.net/milei-prueba-con-malvinas-el-populismo-nacionalista-que-puede-salir-mal.md) - Newsletter semanal correspondiente al 18 de setiembre de 2026\n- [Política de frontera: La IA y la crisis de la forma democrática](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/ia-laboratorio-de-frontera-democracia-openai-amodei-anthropic-politica.md) - Si queremos salvar la democracia, las instituciones del mañana deben moldearse de acuerdo a las posibilidades del mañana\n- [The feminists taking on Germany’s anti-abortion movement](https://www.opendemocracy.net/the-feminists-taking-on-germanys-anti-abortion-movement.md) - Berlin’s March for Life may be getting smaller, but activists warn it is more politically powerful\n- [Las feministas que enfrentan al movimiento antiabortista en Alemania](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/alemania-feministas-heartbeat-international-desinformacion-aborto.md) - La Marcha por la Vida de Berlín convoca a menos gente, pero las activistas feministas advierten que su poder político va en aumento\n- [AI’s data centre construction boom is crushing workers](https://www.opendemocracy.net/ais-data-centre-construction-boom-is-crushing-workers.md) - As data centre companies rake in business, workers say they are being pushed to the limit.\n- [A progressive alliance is now critical to counter a Farage government](https://www.opendemocracy.net/progressive-left-alliance-critical-to-counter-farage-government-reform-2029.md) - With billionaire donors bankrolling Reform, the fractured left must form a coalition ahead of the next election\n- [Malvinas y la batalla de la extrema derecha argentina por la memoria](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es/argentina-milei-malvinas-reino-unido-soberania-ultraderecha-villarruel-memoria.md) - El reclamo de soberanía sobre las Islas Malvinas pasa de causa nacional a herramienta política de Milei\n- [I study political messaging. Here's what is hurting Reform](https://www.opendemocracy.net/reform-uk-nigel-farage-crypto-financial-scandals-polls-rating-fall-why-persuasion-uk.md) - Our research shows Nigel Farage’s anti-elitist brand is vulnerable to stories linking billionaire cash to party policy\n- [‘Silence is not neutrality’: Organising against the far right in Saxony-Anhalt](https://www.opendemocracy.net/silence-is-not-neutrality-organising-against-the-far-right-in-saxony-anhalt.md) - After the AfD’s win, activists say resisting the far right means defending the institutions where its politics take hold\n- [Hundreds of abuse victims arrested when calling for help, new data finds](https://www.opendemocracy.net/domestic-abuse-victims-jail-theresa-may-conservatives.md) - openDemocracy’s reporting praised at parliamentary event on abuse victims arrested for assaulting emergency workers\n- [9/11 revisited + UK’s sovereign AI chief joins US AI company](https://www.opendemocracy.net/weekly-email-120926.md) - openDemocracy Weekly Newsletter 12 September 2026\n- [¿Es Venezuela nuestro canario en la mina de carbón?](https://www.opendemocracy.net/es-venezuela-nuestro-canario-en-la-mina-de-carbon.md) - Newsletter semanal correspondiente al 11 de setiembre de 2026\n- [Trump’s Venezuela: Wh